Good — I opened and checked the files, Sir.

What I inspected
- prototype-jason-ui/script.js — I confirmed you stored the initializer as window.jasonSttTts and added the speak(...) call after appendMessage. Good.
- prototype-jason-ui/index.html — I confirmed script.js loads before stt_tts_bridge.js (bridge is still included after script.js).

Why it may still not speak
- Timing: if for any reason the bridge object (window.JasonSTTTS) isn't present when your DOMContentLoaded handler runs, your init code will silently skip, leaving window.jasonSttTts undefined. With scripts in the body the browser usually executes both before DOMContentLoaded, but race conditions or different hosting setups can still cause the bridge to be unavailable at that exact moment.
- Autoplay / user-gesture policies: less likely since demo.html works for you, but possible differences in how prototype-jason-ui triggers speak (automatic vs after a gesture).
- Silent failures: speak(...) might be called but failing silently — adding a short log around the call helps confirm.

Quick checks you can run now (paste in DevTools console)
1) Is the bridge and instance present?
